  "native_rules": [
    "The actual normal player swap prepares both special models, classifies combo9 as move1, consumes exactly one move and records native session combo9 once. Prepare places the propeller at the native from-cell, detaches the actual rocket and stops its creation animation.",
    "Loop296 and haptic30/type2/0.7 run at activation. The emptied cell freezes for0.15. The primary strategy retains the existing rocket orientation: horizontal0 uses trigger11/operation10, vertical1 uses trigger10/operation11.",
    "Line scoring uses native current-item scores, per-line goal admission, signed32-bit sums and the original positive-lightball penalty. Winning lines override score selection; ordinary ties consume one RNG draw, useful negative lines retain first strict maximum, and the selected line receives forward Fisher-Yates shuffling before positive/valid-target selection.",
    "The normal single score list fills before rocket line selection, with the original single-target fallback if a line cannot supply a target. Target reservations keep the native guided1/2 identities. Area selection also retains its native single fallback.",
    "The actual shared PropellerSpecialComboPilot carries the real rocket prefab. Native front/back sorting, counter-moving roots, Quintic/SmoothDamp scaling,5-degree rocket root rotation and60/255 shadow alpha run with the existing primary homing pilot. TNT retains10-degree rotation.",
    "Only trigger10 freezes cross fall for the selected target column. Straight fall remains allowed. Arrival uses an application-owned Unity wait0.07 before releasing all column freezes; its coroutine lifetime is independent of game-context dispatch.",
    "Arrival detaches the rocket to the actual board root and resets its root transform/scale. The strategy hides the actual rocket, yields Unity WaitForSeconds0.07, shows it and executes the orientation-specific rocket explosion. The combo operation independently finishes after0.5 gameplay seconds.",
    "Propeller arrival plays the restored original seven-system PropellerRocketComboParticles prefab through native global pool13, prewarmed once and reused. Both actual rocket halves retain native flight/damage/unfreeze and view-tail recycling; no shortened lifetime is introduced to satisfy a test.",
    "Sixteen consecutive recorded-input swaps exercise two rocket orientations, both moving-item roles and four gesture directions. They verify actual carrying/root motion/sorting, arrival hide/delay, reservations, column freeze release, two-half travel, box goals, refill, one move, subsequent input and completed view/global-particle pool ownership.",
